sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch01-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch01-03--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch01-03--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch01-03: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.24" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.243"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.62"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The mechanism can be stated in modern variables, as environmentally induced germline change versus ordinary mutation. Public archives do not contain the paired measurements that would show it is the most frequent cause, or that the reproductive system is uniquely sensitive, across animals and plants under domestication. A test would require new compilation at best and new designs for most species." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Measure the share of new heritable variation attributable to pre-conception environmental effects on gametes, relative to spontaneous mutation and recombination, across domesticated and confined species, and compare environmental sensitivity of reproductive failure with sensitivity of other organ systems. The reproductive-element account would be supported if that pathway explained more new variation than the alternatives and if reproduction failed under milder environmental change than other systems." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "No open database records pre-conception environments, gamete state, and offspring heritable variance for the same individuals.", "Zoo and studbook reproductive-failure records that might speak to sensitivity of the reproductive system are not generally public.", "Epigenetic and mutation-rate studies cover a few model species and are not harmonized." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch01-03--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch01-03 by Grok 4.7: 0.5" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
